-- title:
--   Gauss prolongations exhaust the valuation rings of L
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by $p$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\iota_O(O) \subseteq A$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let `data` be modular polynomial data for $p$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(p)$ vanishing on the pair of $q$-expansions), let `hKr` be the Kronecker congruence asserting that $\Phi$ reduced modulo $p$ equals $(C X^p - X)(C X - X^p)$, and let `hα`, `hβ` be the integrality of the Hecke homomorphisms $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$, $\mathrm{heckeBetaBar}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at level $1$ and prime $p$. Let $P$ be a place specialisation of these data and $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, furnishing two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(p)) =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` with residue field `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField A) 1`. Let $L$ be a field with a ring homomorphism $\varphi : L \to \overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(p))$, a homomorphism $\theta_O : O \to L$ with $\varphi \circ \theta_O$ equal to $\iota_O$ followed by the constants, and a homomorphism $\theta_F$ from `modularFunctionFieldFull p` to $L$ such that $\varphi(\theta_F f)$ is, as a Laurent series, the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $f$; assume the subfield of $L$ generated by the ranges of $\theta_F$ and $\theta_O$ is all of $L$. Finally let $\mathcal V$ be a valuation subring of $L$ such that $p$ is a nonunit of $\mathcal V$, every nonzero $g \in \mathcal V$ is of the form $p^n u$ with $u$ a unit of $\mathcal V$, $\theta_O(O) \subseteq \mathcal V$, and for every $Q \in \mathbb Z[X]$ whose reduction modulo $p$ is nonzero both $Q(\theta_F(jq))$ and its inverse lie in $\mathcal V$. Then $\mathcal V$ equals the preimage under $\varphi$ of $R_1$'s valuation ring of integers, or the preimage of $R_2$'s.
--
--   This is the valuation-theoretic form of the identification of the local rings at the generic points of the two branches of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over an unramified discrete valuation ring with the two Gauss prolongations: here $L$ plays the role of the function field of the base-changed model and $\mathcal V$ of a vertical local ring. It is used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport model package, where the stalk of $\varphi$ at a specialised point is shown to lie in one of the two prolongations and to be expressible through the $j$-function.
